                    briefing_text_r3:       `The story has run; now turn inward. The rumour mill is hot and <strong>silence feeds it</strong> — say nothing and the channel fills the void with “leadership knew” and “the analyst is being sacrificed”. But <em>over-disclosing</em> unproven claims during a live review contaminates the investigation and exposes the analyst. Find the calibrated line: brief the 48 early and honestly, decide how to handle the anonymous channel, and <strong>protect the named analyst</strong> with support and due process — never pre-judging, never scapegoating. How you treat the leaker and the analyst is what the other 47 are watching; it either reinforces psychological safety or destroys it.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Sustain energy & rebuild trust`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `The news cycle has passed. Now convert a reputational hit into restored trust over the coming weeks. Two senior consultants — <strong>£1.4M of billing</strong> — are wavering and built their loyalty on the belief that this place protects its people; keep them with commitments you can <em>actually honour</em>, not promises that betray them twice when the review lands elsewhere. Make a fair, transparent decision on the analyst and name the systemic lesson. Commit a <strong>real methodology-governance fix</strong> — not a cosmetic refresh — and invest genuinely in wellbeing and re-engagement to recover the score. Prove the fix is real, not theatre.`,

                    r1_frame_label:         `How do you frame this crisis to your leadership group?`,
                    frame_coupled:          `One crisis with two faces — the leak couples reputation and internal trust; manage both together`,
                    frame_external:         `A media problem — handle the press now, deal with the team next week`,
                    frame_internal:         `An HR problem — find and discipline the leaker, the press will pass`,
                    frame_overblown:        `Overblown — one journalist, one anonymous source; ride it out`,
                    r1_verify_label:        `Before any public word, what do you establish about the allegation?`,
                    verify_verify:          `Separate true / contested / unknown — quietly check whether the analyst really was pressured`,
                    verify_false:           `Assume it's false — our methodology is sound, build the rebuttal`,
                    verify_true:            `Assume it's true — pre-emptively concede everything to look transparent`,
                    verify_ignore:          `Don't investigate — knowing less protects deniability`,
                    r1_attention_label:     `How much leadership attention goes to wellbeing & the rumour mill from hour one? (%)`,
                    r1_attention_readout:   `Internal-trust attention (vs press-only focus):`,

                    r2_posture_label:       `With the clock running, choose the public posture (SCCT):`,
                    posture_ack:            `Acknowledge & investigate — confirm an independent review, commit to publish findings`,
                    posture_limited:        `Limited statement — take the allegation seriously, say little until facts are in`,
                    posture_deny:           `Flat denial — categorically reject the allegation before the review concludes`,
                    posture_nocomment:      `No comment — decline to engage and let the story run`,
                    r2_client_label:        `What do you tell the £26M public-sector clients before the story breaks?`,
                    client_prebrief:        `Pre-brief them honestly — own the review, share the facts and the remediation plan`,
                    client_reassure:        `Reassure only — tell them it's baseless, no detail`,
                    client_silence:         `Say nothing — let them learn it from the newspaper`,
                    r2_consistency_label:   `How tightly must the public line match what the internal review can stand behind? (%)`,
                    r2_consistency_readout: `Internal-external consistency enforced:`,

                    r3_internal_label:      `What do you communicate to the 48-person team, and when?`,
                    internal_early:         `Brief them early & honestly — name the allegation, the review, and what you can't yet say`,
                    internal_late:          `Wait until the story runs, then explain — keep things tight until then`,
                    internal_silent:        `Say nothing internally — control the message, avoid feeding the rumour`,
                    internal_over:          `Tell them everything — names, suspicions, unproven claims, full transparency now`,
                    r3_channel_label:       `How do you handle the anonymous channel and the rumours?`,
                    channel_engage:         `Engage it openly — answer the “leadership knew” rumour directly, correct falsehoods, invite questions`,
                    channel_monitor:        `Monitor quietly — don't post, but track sentiment and brief leads to answer in person`,
                    channel_shutdown:       `Try to shut it down — hunt the leaker, threaten consequences for posting`,
                    channel_ignore:         `Ignore it — it will burn itself out`,
                    r3_analyst_label:       `How do you protect the named junior analyst?`,
                    analyst_support:        `Support & due process — wellbeing support, fair review, no public blame, no pre-judging`,
                    analyst_scapegoat:      `Distance leadership — frame it as one analyst's error to protect the practice`,
                    analyst_prejudge:       `Pre-judge — publicly clear or condemn them now to settle the rumour`,
                    r3_pace_label:          `How calibrated is your disclosure — enough to slow rumour, not so much it breaks due process? (%)`,
                    r3_pace_readout:        `Calibrated transparency (0 = silence, 100 = broadcast everything):`,

                    r4_retention_label:     `The two senior consultants (£1.4M billing) are wavering. What do you offer?`,
                    retain_honest:          `Honest commitments — fair process, real say in the governance fix, no promises you can't keep`,
                    retain_over:            `Over-promise — guarantee no consequences for anyone and a specific investigation outcome`,
                    retain_nothing:         `Offer nothing specific — assume loyalty will hold`,
                    r4_analystdecision_label: `The review concludes. How do you decide and communicate the analyst's situation?`,
                    decide_fair:            `Fair & transparent — act on the evidence, protect the person, share the systemic lesson`,
                    decide_quiet:           `Handle it quietly — resolve it privately, tell the team nothing`,
                    decide_blame:           `Make an example — discipline visibly to show the firm acted`,
                    r4_governance_label:    `What governance fix do you commit to, to prevent recurrence?`,
                    gov_real:               `Real methodology governance — independent sign-off, audit trail, protected challenge route`,
                    gov_cosmetic:           `A cosmetic policy refresh and a town-hall — signal action, change little`,
                    gov_none:               `No structural fix — it was a one-off, move on`,
                    r4_recovery_label:      `How much do you invest in a genuine wellbeing & re-engagement plan? (%)`,
                    r4_recovery_hint:       `Listening sessions, workload relief, restored psychological safety — drives the engagement recovery.`,

                    warn_attention_range:   `Internal-trust attention must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
                    warn_consistency_range: `Internal-external consistency must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
